  "issue": {
    "body": "We've encountered cases where credentialed requests (ie. with cookies), followed by non-credentialed requests will get an `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header in the response, containing the `Origin` from the previous credentialed request.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport uvicorn\r\n\r\nfrom starlette.applications import Starlette\r\nfrom starlette.responses import PlainTextResponse\r\nfrom starlette.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\r\n\r\n\r\napp = Starlette()\r\napp.add_middleware(\r\n    CORSMiddleware,\r\n    allow_origins=[\"*\"],\r\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\r\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\r\n)\r\n\r\n\r\n@app.route(\"/\")\r\ndef homepage(request):\r\n    return PlainTextResponse(\"Homepage\", status_code=200)\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=5100)\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n1. curl without a cookie, get `access-control-allow-origin: *` back \r\n```\r\n$ curl -v -H 'Origin: https://someplace.org' http://127.0.0.1:5100\r\n* Rebuilt URL to: http://127.0.0.1:5100/\r\n*   Trying 127.0.0.1...\r\n* TCP_NODELAY set\r\n* Connected to 127.0.0.1 (127.0.0.1) port 5100 (#0)\r\n> GET / HTTP/1.1\r\n> Host: 127.0.0.1:5100\r\n> User-Agent: curl/7.54.0\r\n> Accept: */*\r\n> Origin: https://someplace.org\r\n>\r\n< HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n< date: Mon, 13 May 2019 10:32:58 GMT\r\n< server: uvicorn\r\n< content-length: 8\r\n< content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n< access-control-allow-origin: *\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. curl with a cookie, get the Origin header back as `access-control-allow-origin`:\r\n```\r\n$ curl -v -H 'Origin: https://someplace.org' --cookie \"foo=bar\"  http://127.0.0.1:5100\r\n* Rebuilt URL to: http://127.0.0.1:5100/\r\n*   Trying 127.0.0.1...\r\n* TCP_NODELAY set\r\n* Connected to 127.0.0.1 (127.0.0.1) port 5100 (#0)\r\n> GET / HTTP/1.1\r\n> Host: 127.0.0.1:5100\r\n> User-Agent: curl/7.54.0\r\n> Accept: */*\r\n> Cookie: foo=bar\r\n> Origin: https://someplace.org\r\n>\r\n< HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n< date: Mon, 13 May 2019 10:34:10 GMT\r\n< server: uvicorn\r\n< content-length: 8\r\n< content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n< access-control-allow-origin: https://someplace.org\r\n```\r\n\r\n3. curl without the cookie header, get the erroneous `Origin` header from the previous request\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ curl -v -H 'Origin: https://someplace.org' http://127.0.0.1:5100\r\n* Rebuilt URL to: http://127.0.0.1:5100/\r\n*   Trying 127.0.0.1...\r\n* TCP_NODELAY set\r\n* Connected to 127.0.0.1 (127.0.0.1) port 5100 (#0)\r\n> GET / HTTP/1.1\r\n> Host: 127.0.0.1:5100\r\n> User-Agent: curl/7.54.0\r\n> Accept: */*\r\n> Origin: https://someplace.org\r\n>\r\n< HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n< date: Mon, 13 May 2019 10:34:46 GMT\r\n< server: uvicorn\r\n< content-length: 8\r\n< content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n< access-control-allow-origin: https://someplace.org\r\n```",
